    "title": "Free summer concert in Gardner brings Eagles hits to Monument Park - NewsBreak",
    "text": "The Long Run: Songs of the Eagles will perform at the Gardner Summer Concert Series on Aug. 9. According to a community announcement, the concert starts at 6 p.m. at Monument Park, located at Central Street and Route 101. This free event features music from the Eagles, covering their hits from the 1970s to the 1990s. The rain date is set for Aug. 10 at 2 p.m. The band includes Gardner resident Glenn Jackson and Westminster resident Dan Kirouac (formerly of Beatles For Sale), as well as Rick Barrett, Kathy Finn and Carl Bongiovi. Follow the band at https://www.facebook.com/groups/thelongrunmassachusetts . Greater Gardner gears up for summer concerts starting June 14: Check out the lineup This story was created by reporter Beth McDermott, bmcdermott1@gannett.com, with the assistance of Artificial Intelligence (AI). Journalists were involved in every step of the information gathering, review, editing and publishing process. Learn more at https://cm.usatoday.com/ethical-conduct . This article originally appeared on Gardner News: Free summer concert in Gardner brings Eagles hits to Monument Park",
